\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D444 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c22A2\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" space=\"4\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D443 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>∨</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊢</mo><mi>P</mi></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>, and break that sequent.</li>\n<li>Give a correct derivation.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch2/reductio-and-classical-rules.html"}